meta {
  name: Download Resume
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}{{apiPrefix}}/resume/download
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  # Download Resume

  The one endpoint that does not answer with the response envelope: it is a
  **302** to a Cloudinary URL carrying `fl_attachment`, so the browser saves the
  file instead of rendering it.

  The website links to this directly with a plain anchor. Do not fetch it as a
  blob from JavaScript: that buffers the whole PDF in memory, throws away the
  `Content-Disposition` filename, and makes the download depend on Cloudinary's
  CORS policy.

  The redirect target includes the stored Cloudinary `version`, so replacing the
  resume changes the URL and no CDN or browser serves the old PDF.

  Bruno follows redirects, so the response body here is the PDF itself.

  | Status | Meaning |
  | --- | --- |
  | 302 | redirect to the PDF |
  | 503 | `RESUME_NOT_CONFIGURED` — nothing uploaded yet, see **Upload Resume** |
  | 503 | `CLOUDINARY_NOT_CONFIGURED` |
}
